load @term/seed/structure/field
  find field

# A field, the concept: a set where addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division (except by zero) all work, so
# every nonzero element has a multiplicative inverse. The rationals, the reals, and the complex numbers are fields, and
# they are the scalars an algebra is built over. The first two rungs of the number tower, the reals and the complex
# numbers, are fields; the quaternions lose commutativity and become a division ring instead. The canonical field form
# is in the structure folder.
form field-concept
  link structure, like field
